# {{ .Title }}

> {{ .Blurb }}

Commands are driven from a terminal by developers and AI agents; the tracker
keeps its own web UI for everybody else. The backend is the source of truth,
so every write goes straight to it and reads are cached for one minute. Claims
are soft, expiring locks that keep two agents off the same ticket.

Authentication is delegated: yakanban stores no credentials and falls back to
`gh auth token`, so a run without a token environment variable and without the
GitHub CLI on PATH exits 4.

This file is generated from the repository's own sources at build time. It
describes {{ .Title }} {{ .Version }}.

